        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "This sari was made at Benares (Varanasi), an important centre of fine weaving from ancient times, developed as a silk weaving centre during the Mughal period. It still has many fine silk weaving workshops. Black and dark blue fabrics patterned with gold are often used at Diwali, the Hindu Festival of Light."@en ;
